Query:
"issue, when token is refreshed at about 6 AM, logs files got deleted for yeasterday or wiped out, so logs of whatsapp BOT (specially SILVERM which closes at 11:30) so for whatsapp i want logs to retained for 2 days so as it will be downloaded and renamed arraneed in yeasterdaty and todays (please see logic)!! please suggest better method!! i think when laptop lid is open we download BOT logs at 5 PM o al yestaersy logs are preserved!!"

Logic:
1. In `sync_master.sh`, `split_logs_by_date()` reads live rolling logs (e.g. `silverm.log`, `app.log`) and uses awk to extract lines into daily files formatted as `<base>_DDMonYY.log`.
2. When a rolling log rotated (e.g. `silverm.log` rotating to `silverm.log.1`), `split_logs_by_date()` only processed the active `silverm.log`, ignoring `silverm.log.1`.
3. Because awk's `print > out` truncates the destination file on its initial write, processing only the newly-rotated active log caused the daily file (e.g. `silverm_19Nov26.log`) to be overwritten with only the post-rotation lines, dropping the earlier session lines.
4. Updated `split_logs_by_date()` in `/Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/MAC/sync_master.sh` to assemble an input array `LOG_INPUTS`: if `${LOG_FILE}.1` exists, it is passed first, followed by `$LOG_FILE`.
5. This guarantees all lines from both the rotated segment and active segment are parsed in chronological order, seamlessly rebuilding complete daily logs for yesterday and today without data loss.

Final Code Change:
- Modified `/Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/MAC/sync_master.sh` inside `split_logs_by_date()`: Constructed `LOG_INPUTS` array checking for `${LOG_FILE}.1`, passing `"${LOG_INPUTS[@]}"` into the awk script instead of `$LOG_FILE` alone.
- Verified syntax with `bash -n /Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/MAC/sync_master.sh`.
- Verified live split on `/Users/vivek/ICICI_Direct/Google/whatsapp`: `silverm_19Nov26.log` expanded from 9.9 KB to 561 KB, capturing all daytime and evening lines, and `silverm_18Nov26.log` completed at 869 KB.

